1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,400
y = mx + b. What is it FOR? You wondered at 14. Nobody answered.

2
00:00:02,400 --> 00:00:05,600
A small shop. Four days of sales: 30, 40, 50, 60.

3
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:08,800
Four dots on a graph. x is the day, y is the sales. That is all the data.

4
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:12,000
Look at the step from one day to the next. Ten more. Ten more. Ten more.

5
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,200
It never changes. That step is m. m = 10.

6
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:18,400
Join the dots and you get one straight line.

7
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:21,600
Run it backwards, past day one, to where it started: 20. That is b. b = 20.

8
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:25,600
So the line is y = 10x + 20. The step is 10, the start is 20. Two numbers — that is the entire line.

9
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:28,800
Now run it one more day. Day 5: ten times five, plus twenty.

10
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:31,200
Seventy. Tomorrow you sell 70. You just predicted the future.

11
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:34,800
We learned this at school. Nobody ever said what for.

12
00:00:34,800 --> 00:00:38,400
Pause. Observe. Learn. Follow for the math behind AI — @observer.collapse
